{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NMRgwPyRwy4nxppbqsAgtd","type":"tool_result","content":"file\t17587\tlib/hub/README.md\nfile\t13624\tlib/hub/bridge.js\ndir\t0\tlib/hub/examples\nfile\t27469\tlib/hub/harness.html\nfile\t3718\tlib/hub/retrofit.md\nfile\t20248\tlib/hub/round.js\nfile\t16707\tlib/hub/session.js\n---\n{\"assets\":[{\"name\":\"pixel-engine.zip\",\"size\":2716491}],\"body\":\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0 as the engine kit: `pixel-engine.zip` below holds the engine as one ES module, its guides, a starter game and `check.mjs`. Unzip it, then read `README.md` and `GUIDE.md`.\\n\\nThe newest release is always https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip; this one stays at https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/download/engine-v0.46.0/pixel-engine.zip.\\n\\n## What changed in 0.46.0\\n\\n- **No more handoff page**: the engine's site is gone, so `manifest.json` has no `handoff` and the\\n  kit's `README.md` no longer names a page for agents. Newer kits are where they were:\\n  `latest` (the newest release's zip), `releases` and `source`.\\n\",\"name\":\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0\",\"published\":\"2026-11-02T14:27:22Z\",\"tag\":\"engine-v0.46.0\"}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"02cb6029-d990-4c3d-8317-1547846d1bc4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:17.327Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"file\t17587\tlib/hub/README.md\nfile\t13624\tlib/hub/bridge.js\ndir\t0\tlib/hub/examples\nfile\t27469\tlib/hub/harness.html\nfile\t3718\tlib/hub/retrofit.md\nfile\t20248\tlib/hub/round.js\nfile\t16707\tlib/hub/session.js\n---\n{\"assets\":[{\"name\":\"pixel-engine.zip\",\"size\":2716491}],\"body\":\"Pixel Engine 0.46.0 as the engine kit: `pixel-engine.zip` below holds the engine as one ES module, its guides, a starter game and `check.mjs`. Unzip it, then read `README.md` and `GUIDE.md`.\\n\\nThe newest release is always https://g