{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DxYmCNq3nzBFVxkyuy5pv6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# The library (Pixel Engine 0.46.0)\n2\t\n3\tEvery built-in model (`MODEL_LIBRARY`, 151) and texture (`TEXTURE_LIBRARY`, 126) by family, then every imported pack (575 models, 264 textures in `packs/`), generated from the defs. A model's variants (`rock-large-a` … `-f`) share a row. Search it; don't read it whole.\n4\t\n5\t- **Find:** grep this file, filter `library.json` (one record per asset: id, kind, family, pack, tags, size, licence), or search in code: `MODEL_LIBRARY.search('wooden chair')`, `TEXTURE_LIBRARY.search('stone floor')` (ranked: id words, then tags, then about; plurals and parts of words count).\n6\t- **Place:** `buildModel(id, { params, palette })`, or `use` it inside your own models; textures with `textureMap(id)`, `spriteSheet(id)`, `hudSprite(id)`. Look at it first: `node check.mjs --sheets <id>` (ASSETS.md).\n7\t- **Packs** are someone else's work, imported into this format and palette: each section says how to load it, and CREDITS.md what its licence asks. Its rows leave out the pack's name and tags, which library.json keeps.\n8\t\n9\t## Models\n10\t\n11\t### architecture (19)\n12\t\n13\t| id | size (m, w × h × d) | params: default (min–max) | palette slots | tags | about |\n14\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n15\t| `door` | 1.48 × 2.2 × 0.32 |  | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, wood orange, wood2 red, iron night, brass sand | architecture, stone, wood | Plank door 2.2 m tall in a stone frame; the leaf is a pivot (`leaf`) hinged on the left, with iron straps and a brass ring handle |\n16\t| `window` | 2 × 2.26 × 0.42 | width 0.8 (0.4–2), height 1 (0.5–1.8) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, wood orange, wood2 red, glass navy, iron night | architecture, stone, wood | Framed window with a cross mullion, a stone sill and lintel and two plank shutters open flat, in a short stone wall |\n17\t| `column` | 0.6 × 2.6 × 0.6 | height 2.6 (1–5) | stone mist, stone2 slate | architecture, stone | Stone column: a square plinth and moulded base, a tapering shaft, a flared capital under a square abacus |\n18\t| `stairs` | 1.2 × 1.08 × 1.8 | steps 6 (2–16), width 1.2 (0.6–3), rise 0.18 (0.12–0.25) | stone mist, stone2 slate | architecture, stone | Flight of stone steps climbing toward the back (-Z), one box per step from the floor, shades alternating so each edge reads |\n19\t| `fence` | 3.12 × 1.02 × 0.18 | length 3 (1–8) | wood orange, wood2 red | architecture, wood | Wooden fence along X: square posts with pyramid caps about every metre, two rails nailed across their fronts |\n20\t| `roof` | 4.7 × 1.73 × 3.73 | width 4 (1.5–10), depth 3 (1.5–8), pitch 40 (15–60) | tile red, tile2 plum, stone mist, wood orange | architecture, roof, stone, wood | Gable roof to sit on walls (y = 0 is the wall top): two pitched slabs of tile courses, stone gable ends, a ridge beam |\n21\t| `gate` | 1.52 × 1.45 × 0.17 |  | wood orange, wood2 red, iron night | architecture, wood | Wooden yard gate between two capped posts: a picket leaf (pivot `leaf`, hinged on the left) with rails, a brace and an iron latch |\n22\t| `stone-wall` | 2 × 3 × 0.3 | length 2 (0.5–6), height 3 (0.5–5) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night | architecture, stone, wall, modular | Modular stone wall along X, `length` x 0.3 m centred on the origin, `height` 3 m to a storey: blocks in two shaded courses over dark mortar (one course alternates its blocks); its ends meet the next piece so the bond runs on across pieces set end to end on the 1 m grid |\n23\t| `wall-corner` | 1.21 × 3 × 1.21 | arm 1 (0.5–3), height 3 (0.5–5) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, dressed sand | architecture, stone, wall, modular | Corner of the modular stone walls: a pier of dressed quoins on the origin, two `arm` m arms along -X and -Z (footprint 1.2 x 1.2 m at the default), `height` 3 m; turn it in 90-degree steps |\n24\t| `doorway` | 2 × 3 × 0.4 | length 2 (1.5–5), height 3 (2.7–5) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, dressed sand | architecture, stone, wall, modular | Modular stone wall along X (`length` x 0.3 m, like `stone-wall`) with a 1 m wide, 2.3 m high opening under a dressed lintel, open to colliders so actors walk through |\n25\t| `wide-window` | 3 × 3 × 0.46 | length 3 (2–5), height 3 (2.7–5) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, dressed sand, glass navy | architecture, stone, wall, modular | Modular stone wall along X (`length` x 0.3 m, like `stone-wall`) with a window as wide as the wall less a block each side and three courses tall: glass between dressed mullions, a sill and a lintel; the glazed window blocks like the wall (its glass collides); map `glass` |\n26\t| `ruined-wall` | 2 × 1.84 × 0.3 | length 2 (1–5), height 2.25 (1–3) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night | architecture, stone, wall, ruin, modular | Ruin of the modular stone wall along X, `length` x 0.3 m: its courses broken off to a seeded jagged top under `height`, deepest at a seeded point; add `rubble` at its foot |\n27\t| `balcony` | 2 × 1.98 × 1.04 | width 2 (1–4), depth 1 (0.6–1.5) | wood orange, wood2 red, frame plum | architecture, wood, town, modular | Wooden balcony to hang on a wall at z = 0, its deck 3 m up (a storey of `stone-wall`): boards on joists and knee braces, a baluster railing round three sides; footprint `width` x `depth` m |\n28\t| `bridge` | 3 × 0.96 × 1.61 | length 3 (1–8), width 1.6 (1–3) | wood orange, wood2 red, beam plum | architecture, wood, nature, town, modular | Wooden footbridge span along X, `length` x `width` m: seeded planks laid across two dark beams whose feet rest on the banks at y = 0, the deck 0.32 m up, a dark rail on low posts along each side; the deck carries actors and the rails stop them |\n29\t| `chimney` | 1.06 × 3.14 × 0.76 | height 2.5 (1–5) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, dressed sand, pot orange, flue ink | architecture, stone, roof, town | Stone chimney stack, 0.9 x 0.6 m and `height` to its dressed cap: coursed blocks over mortar, two clay pots with dark flues; stand it against a gable or on a ridge |\n30\t| `battlement` | 3 × 1.83 × 0.42 | merlons 3 (1–8) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, dressed sand, slit ink | architecture, stone, wall, castle, modular | Crenellated parapet to sit on a wall top (y = 0 there): a dressed string course, a coursed breast wall and coping, `merlons` slit merlons one to each metre with half a crenel at each end so pieces line up; footprint `merlons` x 0.42 m |\n31\t| `trapdoor` | 1 × 0.12 × 1 | open 0 (0–110) | wood orange, wood2 red, frame plum, iron night, ring sand, pit ink | architecture, wood, dungeon, floor | Trapdoor on the floor, 1 x 1 m: a frame round a plank hatch with iron strap hinges and a brass ring, on the pivot `hatch` hinged at the back; `open` (degrees) lifts it off a dark pit that stays open to colliders |\n32\t| `stone-steps` | 2.06 × 1.4 × 2.04 | steps 5 (2–12), width 1.4 (0.8–3) | stone mist, stone2 slate, cheek night, dressed sand | architecture, stone, town, modular | Stone steps up to a landing: `steps` risers of 0.2 m climbing toward -Z between dark cheek walls with dressed copings, a 1 m landing at the back; footprint 2 x 2 m at the defaults |\n33\t| `timber-wall` | 2 × 3 × 0.3 | length 2 (1–4), height 3 (2–4) | plaster white, plate ink, beam plum, stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night | architecture, wood, wall, town, modular | Timber-frame wall panel along X (Tudor), `length` x 0.3 m, `height` 3 m to a storey: white plaster between dark posts, plates, a rail and braces on a course of stone in two shades; lines up with `stone-wall` |\n34\t\n35\t### containers (10)\n36\t\n37\t| id | size (m, w × h × d) | params: default (min–max) | palette slots | tags | about |\n38\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n39\t| `barrel` | 0.73 × 0.82 × 0.73 |  | wood orange, band slate, lid red | container, wood | Wooden barrel with three iron ho