{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PxWRJSM7CUHPj6U8qPycXH","type":"tool_result","content":"10://   node check.mjs --headless game.js    play the game in Node, no browser: steps, errors, a replay\n23://   --headless [game.js]             play a game module in Node with Engine.headless instead of a\n31:// It needs Node 20.15+ (or 22.2+) and, except for --headless, Playwright (`npm i -D playwright` then\n33:// `playwright-core` with CHROMIUM_PATH set to a Chromium (its headless shell,\n34:// `chrome-linux/headless_shell`, is the lightest): it plays WebGPU on SwiftShader with no\n56:const FLAG = new Set(['cameras', 'help', 'headless']);\n78:const headless = opts.headless === true;\n79:if (headless && (sheets || opts.cameras || opts.looks)) fail('--headless plays the game in Node, with no pictures: --sheets, --cameras and --looks need the browser');\n80:const target = positional[0] ?? (headless ? 'game.js' : 'index.html');\n207:// which the headless shell needs to present\n208:const ARGS = ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu', '--enable-features=Vulkan', '--use-vulkan=swiftshader', '--use-angle=swiftshader', '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'];\n221: * --headless: the game in Node (Engine.headless), no browser. The engine is the pixel-engine.js the\n227:  if (!/\\.m?js$/.test(path)) fail(`--headless plays a game module (game.js), not ${file}: pages need the browser (no --headless)`);\n231:  const report = { ok: false, mode: 'headless', module: relative(process.cwd(), path) || file, keys: opts.keys ?? '*90', frames: 0, fingerprint: null, replayed: null,\n236:    console.log(`check.mjs --headless ${report.module}: ${report.frames} frames in Node${report.status ? `, ${report.status}` : ''}`);\n259:  if (!make) fail(`${file} exports no createGame(): --headless makes the game with it, a fresh one for the replay (GUIDE.md section 8)`);\n266:    engine = await within(Engine.headless(make(), { assets: read, viewport: { width: vw, height: vh, dpr: 1 } }), 'the game\\'s start');\n292:if (headless) await runHeadless(target);\n296:async function launch(server) {\n298:    // headless (Playwright's headless launch is Chromium's headless shell): no display needed\n299:    return await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined, args: ARGS, headless: true });\n327:  const browser = await launch(server);\n448:const browser = await launch(server);\n505:      const frame = await e.renderer.capture();\n### HERO_CLIPS\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_CLIPS: readonly ClipDef[]\n```\n\n### HERO_MODEL\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_MODEL: \"assets/hero.glb\"\n```\n\n### HERO_RAGDOLL\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_RAGDOLL: readonly RagdollPart[]\n```\n\nThe hero as a ragdoll (the joints of `hero.glb`, see rig.ts): pelvis, torso and head, upper\narms and legs on ball joints held in cones, elbows and knees as hinges bending the way the\nclips bend them (Forearm −X, Shin +X). Hands and feet ride on their forearm and shin.\n\n### HERO_RIG\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_RIG: RigSpec\n```\n\nThe hero rig (public/assets/hero.glb, built by scripts/assets/hero.mjs).\n\nThe character faces +Z. L/R are the character's own sides (its right = -X).\nRotations are Euler XYZ degrees relative to rest; Z is applied first, then Y, then X,\nall about the parent's axes. Verified against contact sheets (`npm run anim -- sheet`).\n\n  Pelvis   +X tip forward (90 = face down, -90 = on its back, 360 = front flip)\n           +Y turn to its left, +Z roll to its RIGHT. p = [x, y, z] offset (m), s = squash\n  Torso    +X bend forward, +Y twist left, +Z lean right\n/**\n * Things that sway in the wind: a copy of a mesh's material whose vertex shader leans\n * everything above a height along the wind, more the higher it is (squared: a trunk stays\n * put, the crown moves), with a slow sway, a faster flutter and its own phase. One shared\n * `WindUniforms` drives every swaying thing in a level, so a gust moves them all together.\n *\n *   const wind = new WindUniforms();\n *   swayObject(treeModel, wind, { height: 3, amount: 0.25, phase: 1.7 });\n *   // per frame: wind.update(time, [2, 0.5])\n */\nimport type { Material, Object3D } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { Vector2 } from 'three/webgpu';\nexport declare class WindUniforms {\n    readonly time: any;\n    readonly wind: any;\n    /** Per frame (game time); `wind` along x and z (its length is the strength). */\n    update(time: number, wind: Vector2 | readonly [number, number]): void;\n}\nexport interface SwayOptions {\n    /** Height (in the mesh's own units) of its top: the lean is 0 at `base` and full there. */\n    height: number;\n    /** Where the lean starts (the trunk below stays still). Default 0. */\n    base?: number;\n    /** Lean at the top per unit of wind. Default 0.15. */\n    amount?: number;\n    /** Its own phase (radians): neighbours don't move in lockstep. */\n    phase?: number;\n}\n/**\n * A room-owned copy of `material` that sways. For ordinary meshes: heights are in the mesh's\n * own space (`positionGeometry`), measured from its origin (an instanced mesh would need its\n * own per-instance base).\n */\nexport declare function swayMaterial(material: Material, wind: WindUniforms, o: SwayOptions): Material;\n/** Make every mesh under `root` sway (its materials replaced by swaying copies). */\nexport declare function swayObject(root: Object3D, wind: WindUniforms, o: SwayOptions): void;\n/**\n * Save-states (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1): a running level as data, taken between two\n * frames (`engine.snapshot()`) and put back at once (`engine.restore(snap)`), so restoring a\n * moment no longer means replaying everything before it. The engine keeps its own part (game\n * time, the clock, `ctx.random`, the physics world, the camera, the shake, input still waiting)\n * and the game its own (`Game.snapshot` / `Game.restore`).\n *\n *   const snap = await engine.snapshot();         // JSON: keep it, attach it to a bug\n *   engine.step(300);                             // ...play on\n *   await engine.restore(snap);                   // back to that moment (the same game, loaded)\n *\n * A restore starts the level's recording again from the snapshot (`Recording.from`), so a\n * recording made after one replays with `replay(rec, start)`: it loads the game, restores the\n * snapshot, then plays the frames. docs/engine/determinism.md *Save-states*.\n */\nimport type { CameraRigState } from './camera';\nimport type { ClockState } from './clock';\nimport type { InputState } from './input';\nimport type { PhysicsState } from './physics/Physics';\nimport type { ShakeState } from './shake';\n3:  \"version\": \"0.46.0\",\n6:  \"latest\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"0459b07d-243d-4649-a107-d7ba196a37aa","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:29:05.857Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"10://   node check.mjs --headless game.js    play the game in Node, no browser: steps, errors, a replay\n23://   --headless [game.js]             play a game module in Node with Engine.headless instead of a\n31:// It needs Node 20.15+ (or 22.2+) and, except for --headless, Playwright (`npm i -D playwright` then\n33:// `playwright-core` with CHROMIUM_PATH set to a Chromium (its headless shell,\n34:// `chrome-linux/headless_shell`, is the lightest): it plays WebGPU on SwiftShader with no\n56:const FLAG = new Set(['cameras', 'help', 'headless']);\n78:const headless = opts.headless === true;\n79:if (headless && (sheets || opts.cameras || opts.looks)) fail('--headless plays the game in Node, with no pictures: --sheets, --cameras and --looks need the browser');\n80:const target = positional[0] ?? (headless ? 'game.js' : 'index.html');\n207:// which the headless shell needs to present\n208:const ARGS = ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu', '--enable-features=Vulkan', '--use-vulkan=swiftshader', '--use-angle=swiftshader', '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'];\n221: * --headless: the game in Node (Engine.headless), no browser. The engine is the pixel-engine.js the\n227:  if (!/\\.m?js$/.test(path)) fail(`--headless plays a game module (game.js), not ${file}: pages need the browser (no --headless)`);\n231:  const report = { ok: false, mode: 'headless', module: relative(process.cwd(), path) || file, keys: opts.keys ?? '*90', frames: 0, fingerprint: null, replayed: null,\n236:    console.log(`check.mjs --headless ${report.module}: ${report.frames} frames in Node${report.status ? `, ${report.status}` : ''}`);\n259:  if (!make) fail(`${file} exports no createGame(): --headless makes the game with it, a fresh one for the replay (GUIDE.md section 8)`);\n266:    engine = await within(Engine.headless(make(), { assets: read, viewport: { width: vw, height: vh, dpr: 1 } }), 'the game\\'s start');\n292:if (headless) await runHeadless(target);\n296:async function launch(server) {\n298:    // headless (Playwright's headless launch is Chromium's headless shell): no display needed\n299:    return await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined, args: ARGS, headless: true });\n327:  const browser = await launch(server);\n448:const browser = await launch(server);\n505:      const frame = await e.renderer.capture();\n### HERO_CLIPS\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_CLIPS: readonly ClipDef[]\n```\n\n### HERO_MODEL\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_MODEL: \"assets/hero.glb\"\n```\n\n### HERO_RAGDOLL\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_RAGDOLL: readonly RagdollPart[]\n```\n\nThe hero as a ragdoll (the joints of `hero.glb`, see rig.ts): pelvis, torso and head, upper\narms and legs on ball joints held in cones, elbows and knees as hinges bending the way the\nclips bend them (Forearm −X, Shin +X). Hands and feet ride on their forearm and shin.\n\n### HERO_RIG\n\n```ts\nconst HERO_RIG: RigSpec\n```\n\nThe hero rig (public/assets/hero.glb, built by scripts/assets/hero.mjs).\n\nThe character faces +Z. L/R are the character's own sides (its right = -X).\nRotations are Euler XYZ degrees relative to rest; Z is applied first, then Y, then X,\nall about the parent's axes. Verified against contact sheets (`npm run anim -- sheet`).\n\n  Pelvis   +X tip forward (90 = face down, -90 = on its back, 360 = front flip)\n           +Y turn to its left, +Z roll to its RIGHT. p = [x, y, z] offset (m), s = squash\n  Torso    +X bend forward, +Y twist left, +Z lean right\n/**\n * Things that sway in the wind: a copy of a mesh's material whose vertex shader leans\n * everything above a height along the wind, more the higher it is (squared: a trunk stays\n * put, the crown moves), with a slow sway, a faster flutter and its own phase. One shared\n * `WindUniforms` drives every swaying thing in a level, so a gust moves them all together.\n *\n *   const wind = new WindUniforms();\n *   swayObject(treeModel, wind, { height: 3, amount: 0.25, phase: 1.7 });\n *   // per frame: wind.update(time, [2, 0.5])\n */\nimport type { Material, Object3D } from 'three/webgpu';\nimport { Vector2 } from 'three/webgpu';\nexport declare class WindUniforms {\n    readonly time: any;\n    readonly wind: any;\n    /** Per frame (game time); `wind` along x and z (its length is the strength). */\n    update(time: number, wind: Vector2 | readonly [number, number]): void;\n}\nexport interface SwayOptions {\n    /** Height (in the mesh's own units) of its top: the lean is 0 at `base` and full there. */\n    height: number;\n    /** Where the lean starts (the trunk below stays still). Default 0. */\n    base?: number;\n    /** Lean at the top per unit of wind. Default 0.15. */\n    amount?: number;\n    /** Its own phase (radians): neighbours don't move in lockstep. */\n    phase?: number;\n}\n/**\n * A room-owned copy of `material` that sways. For ordinary meshes: heights are in the mesh's\n * own space (`positionGeometry`), measured from its origin (an instanced mesh would need its\n * own per-instance base).\n */\nexport declare function swayMaterial(material: Material, wind: WindUniforms, o: SwayOptions): Material;\n/** Make every mesh under `root` sway (its materials replaced by swaying copies). */\nexport declare function swayObject(root: Object3D, wind: WindUniforms, o: SwayOptions): void;\n/**\n * Save-states (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1): a running level as data, taken between two\n * frames (`engine.snapshot()`) and put back at once (`engine.restore(snap)`), so restoring a\n * moment no longer means replaying everything before it. The engine keeps its own part (game\n * time, the clock, `ctx.random`, the physics world, the camera, the shake, input still waiting)\n * and the game its own (`Game.snapshot` / `Game.restore`).\n *\n *   const snap = await engine.snapshot();         // JSON: keep it, attach it to a bug\n *   engine.step(300);                             // ...play on\n *   await engine.restore(snap);                   // back to that moment (the same game, loaded)\n *\n * A restore starts the level's recording again from the snapshot (`Recording.from`), so a\n * recording made after one replays with `replay(rec, start)`: it loads the game, restores the\n * snapshot, then plays the frames. docs/engine/determinism.md *Save-states*.\n */\nimport type { CameraRigState } from './camera';\nimport type { ClockState } from './clock';\nimport type { InputState } from './input';\nimport type { PhysicsState } from './physics/Physics';\nimport type { ShakeState } from './shake';\n3:  \"version\": \"0.46.0\",\n6:  \"latest\": \"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PxWRJSM7CUHPj6U8qPycXH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
