{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCe1pvYxuFiEp4JyNPN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019btdFcYZ9846Jh8Vi4uCPd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work; cat > $W/.scratch/spike/patch1.py <<'PY'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    if a not in s: raise SystemExit('NOT FOUND: '+a[:80])\n    s=s.replace(a,b,count)\n\nrep(\"The kit's guide is written with a platformer in mind. These are the traps and answers for a first-person open-world game. I ran all of them. Read `GUIDE.md` whole as the kit asks, and `ASSETS.md` before writing models; search `API.md`, don't read it whole.\",\n    \"The kit's guide is written with a platformer in mind. These are the traps and answers for a first-person open-world game. I ran these unless a line says \\\"not run\\\". Read `GUIDE.md` whole as the kit asks, and `ASSETS.md` before writing models; search `API.md`, don't read it whole.\")\nrep(\"| Esc under pointer lock may never reach you as a keydown | Open the pause menu on `pointerlockchange` to null during play |\",\n    \"| Esc under pointer lock may never reach you as a keydown (browser behaviour, not run here) | Open the pause menu on `pointerlockchange` to null during play |\")\nrep(\"| `requestPointerLock()` can reject shortly after Esc, and an unhandled rejection fails the hub check | Always `.catch(() => {})`. Re-lock from a `pointerup` listener when the game wants the lock |\",\n    \"| `requestPointerLock()` can reject shortly after Esc, and an unhandled rejection fails the hub check (browser behaviour, not run here; the accessor above I ran, but not with a real click) | Always `.catch(() => {})`. Re-lock from a `pointerup` listener when the game wants the lock. Test a real click on a menu item early |\")\nrep(\"The defaults crawl at 7 m/s.\",\"The defaults only reach 7 to 11 m/s on the same ground.\")\nrep(\"{ box:[0.38,0.5,0.22], at:[0,0.25,0], c:'cloth' },\\n      { group:[{ box:[0.2,0.22,0.2]\",\"{ box:[0.38,0.5,0.22], at:[0,0.25,0], c:'cloth' },\\n      { box:[0.06,0.56,0.24], at:[0.1,0.25,0], rot:[0,0,28], c:'strap' },\\n      { group:[{ box:[0.2,0.22,0.2]\")\nrep(\"- Use this soldier as your starting point (it ran; shoulders about 1.12 m, head top about 1.74 m, faces +Z):\",\"- Use this soldier as your starting point (as written it passes `checkModel` with no problems or warnings; shoulders about 1.12 m, head top about 1.74 m, faces +Z):\")\nrep(\"It has A-Z, 0-9 and common punctuation (`. , : ; ! ? ' \\\" - + = / ( ) [ ] { } % # & * @ < > | ~ ^`). There is **no em dash or ellipsis**, so write `-` and `...`; unknown characters draw as `?`.\",\n    \"It has exactly: A-Z, 0-9, space and ``. , : ; ! ? ' \\\" - + = / ( ) [ ] { } % _ # & * @ < > | \\\\ ~ ^ $ ` ° ·`` plus curly quotes. There is **no em dash or ellipsis**, so write `-` and `...`; unknown characters draw as `?`.\")\nrep(\"Add 40 to every height so the ground stays above y = 0 (fog and maths are simpler).\",\"Add 40 to every height so the ground stays above y = 0 (fog and maths are simpler). At wider or narrower screens `hud.width` changes, so anchor HUD items.\") if False else None\nrep(\"Scale 1 is about 28 px tall on a 1080p screen, which I judged readable as the smallest size.\",\"Scale 1 is about 28 px tall on a 1080p screen, which I judged readable as the smallest size. `hud.width` follows the screen's aspect, so anchor everything.\")\nrep(\"**Hub.** I ran the real harness against an engine-weight shared-world page. All four scenarios the hub uses pass in 12 to 17 s, with `AIHub.ready()` called about 3 s after load (one straggler took 6.6 s):\",\n    \"**Hub.** I ran the real harness against an engine-weight shared-world page, with `card:true` and with the `LOOK` from section 6 for the two-player runs. All four scenarios the hub uses pass in 12 to 17 s, with `AIHub.ready()` called about 3 s after load (one straggler took 6.6 s):\")\nrep(\"**Software rendering runs at about 1 fps here.** That is expected. Performance is out of scope: no FPS targets and no optimization. Never judge the game by real time in a headless browser.\",\n    \"**Software rendering runs at about 1 fps here.** That is expected. Treat the performance budget as unlimited: add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights and shadows as a scene needs. FPS targets and optimization are out of scope and handled later. Never judge the game by real time in a headless browser.\")\n# fire\nrep(\"- Each burning cell tries its 8 neighbours with `p = 0.08 * fuelFactor * windFactor * slopeFactor * rainFactor * TUNING.fireSpread`.\",\n    \"- Each burning cell tries its 8 neighbours with `p = 0.02 * fuelFactor * windFactor * slopeFactor * rainFactor * TUNING.fireSpread`, divided by 1.41 for diagonals. I calibrated 0.02 by simulating this grid: on flat grass the head, flank and back of the fire move at 1.9, 1.9, 1.9 m/s with no wind, 3.9, 2.4, 0.35 at 5 m/s, and 4.9, 2.9, 0.4 at 8 m/s. Larger bases run away quickly (0.08 gives about 10 m/s and burns upwind too).\")\nrep(\"- **A test must measure the head of the fire at wind 5 m/s and require 2 to 5 m/s,** with flanks clearly slower, so a sprinting player (7.4 m/s) can escape and a walking one can't.\",\n    \"- **A test must measure the head of the fire at wind 5 m/s and require 2 to 5 m/s,** with flanks clearly slower, so a sprinting or running player can escape and a walking one (3.6 m/s) struggles.\")\n# map coordinates and roads\nrep(\"| Pump Station | (-330, 320) | On the river, feeds Three Wells |\",\"| Pump Station | (-330, 395) | On the river, feeds Three Wells |\")\nrep(\"P3 (210, 130) east road\",\"P3 (170, 90) east road\")\nrep(\"- Mile Forty to P3, the Granary, P6, the Salt Pan.\\n- P3 to East Siding to the Water Tower.\",\n    \"- Mile Forty to P3 to the bridge at (250, 80), then forking to the Granary and to East Siding, then on to the Water Tower.\\n- The Granary to P6 to the Salt Pan.\\n- The back road: Mile Forty over the bridge at (120, 230) to P6.\")\nrep(\"Rails are `mine-rail` pieces or two long boxes. Four **rail halts**\",\"Rails are `mine-rail` pieces or two long boxes, with their own bridge where they cross the river near (270, -5). Four **rail halts**\")\nrep(\"Bridges at (250, 80) and (120, 230); a ford at (-60, 300).\",\"Road bridges at (250, 80) and (120, 230); a ford at (-60, 300), which a track from Mile Forty uses.\")\n# map hand size\nrep(\"Your spike-tested size was too big at 0.62 m.\",\"A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\")\n# boot code\nrep(\"\"\"if (info) {\n  if (!navigator.gpu && !info.server) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\n  const game = createGame({ session: hubSession(info) });        // mode 'round': no title, no menus, no attract\n  if (info.server) { const e = await Engine.headless(game, {}); AIHub.ready(); setInterval(() => e.step(6, 1/60), 100); }\n  else await Engine.start(game, { ...OPTIONS, seed: info.seed });  // game.ready(ctx) calls AIHub.ready() once, with no key press\n} else { /* normal start: touch check, title */ }\"\"\",\n\"\"\"if (info) {\n  const game = createGame({ session: hubSession(info) });        // mode 'round': no title, no menus, no attract\n  if (info.server) { const e = await Engine.headless(game, {}); AIHub.ready(); setInterval(() => e.step(6, 1/60), 100); }\n  else if (!navigator.gpu) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\n  else await Engine.start(game, { ...OPTIONS, seed: info.seed });  // game.ready(ctx) calls AIHub.ready() once, with no key press\n} else { /* normal start: touch check, title */ }\"\"\")\nrep(\"**Listen for Enter and M with a plain `window` keydown listener,** because the harness expects an answer within 3 s and the render loop may be slow.\",\n    \"**Listen for Enter and M with a plain `window` keydown listener** (verified to pass the harness's card check), because the harness expects an answer within 3 s and the render loop may be slow.\")\n# touch detection\nrep(\"**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected.\",\n    \"**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context).\")\nrep(\"   - a phone profile (`p.devices['iPhone 14']` in Chromium with touch): shows the notice and Settings, tap opens Settings, attract runs\",\n    \"   - a phone profile in Chromium (Playwright's `iPhone 14` device, dropping its default browser type, then tap with `page.touchscreen`): shows the notice and Settings, tap opens Settings, attract runs\")\n# build wording\nrep(\"`tools/build.mjs` (verified form; set `OUT` from your brief):\",\"`tools/build.mjs` (the steps I ran, with `</script` escaped; set `OUT` from your brief):\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPY\npython3 $W/.scratch/spike/patch1.py $W/PLAN.md; grep -n \"if False\" $W/.scratch/spike/patch1.py | head -2 >/dev/null; wc -w $W/PLAN.md; grep -n \"Add 40 to every height\" $W/PLAN.md | cut -c1-160","description":"Apply verified corrections to the plan","timeout":30000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1619,"cache_read_input_tokens":459227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1619},"output_tokens":50,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"e4f8504a-4ec0-40e1-8382-7fd19dd3196f","timestamp