{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCh8qSQupbjGXyxsGH7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017eyTHubaEsCJK9Vwy2iYMJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work/PLAN.md","offset":459,"limit":340},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14868,"cache_read_input_tokens":470819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14868},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"3e071734-cb94-4ce7-9647-10009dd6c15d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:08:19.216Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCh8Zp6SaiuewUzh5hN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017eyTHubaEsCJK9Vwy2iYMJ":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work/PLAN.md","offset":459,"limit":340}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017eyTHubaEsCJK9Vwy2iYMJ","type":"tool_result","content":"459\t  Keyed with the hands rig (section 21), with pixel blood, sound and a grunt. These are a highlight, so make them good.\n460\t- **Burning:** catching fire does 8 HP/s plus orange flames at the screen edge until you leave fuel for 2 s or reach water.\n461\t- **Down at 0:** if a buddy is available, a rescue scene plays (section 12). Otherwise: *YOU DIED IN THE SORREL. THE PAPERWORK WILL TAKE LONGER.* Then Continue (last save) or Title.\n462\t\n463\t**Blackwater fever.** The source's malaria idea, with a clock you can feel.\n464\t- `TUNING.feverMinutes` (default 12) ± 2 between attacks; the interval shrinks by 1 minute after each act. First attack scripted in M0.\n465\t- **Onset:** view sways, `chromatic.spread` climbs to 4, saturation falls, warmth up, heartbeat, a line in the subtitle band (*THE FEVER.* or variants), and the prompt `[glyph] TABLET`.\n466\t- **With a tablet** (D-pad Down/H, hold 1 s, hand-to-mouth animation): clears over 5 s.\n467\t- **Ignored for 25 s, or no tablets:** vision narrows, you fall, and you wake at the nearest safehouse or the clinic hours later, with 20% of your stones gone. Buddy if available: they carry you and complain.\n468\t- **Supply:** 3 after M1; Mercy Runs pay 4 each (section 13). Tablets can't be bought with stones. That is the point: Odile wants your time.\n469\t\n470\t---\n471\t\n472\t## 10. Soldiers and AI\n473\t\n474\t**Bodies:** the soldier model in faction palettes (several `skin` values and hat variants), a rifle parented to `HandR`, a `CharacterController` capsule (speed from role), `physics.tag(collider, 'npc')` and a `Map` from collider handle to actor. Clips are in section 21.\n475\t\n476\t**Roles:** rifle (most), mg (slower, heavier burst), sniper (towers, long range), rocket (rare), driver.\n477\t\n478\t**Perception.**\n479\t- Vision cone 120°, range `TUNING.enemyVision` (90 m) × stance (crouch 0.55, in tall grass 0.6) × light (night 0.45, doubled if you are lit by fire or muzzle flash).\n480\t- LOS by `physics.castRay` to head and chest.\n481\t- A suspicion meter fills over about 1.5 s by distance. States: `idle → suspicious → alert → searching → idle`.\n482\t- Hearing: gunshot radius per weapon (rifle 120 m), sprint 40 m, run 25 m.\n483\t- Squad members share the last known position.\n484\t- Close by, a small pixel `?` or `!` floats over the head (HUD text projected through the camera). That is the only detection UI.\n485\t\n486\t**Hostility.** Everyone outside Mile Forty shoots you on sight, with one exception: **while you hold a contract from a faction, you carry its pass**, and its soldiers leave you alone unless you fire near them or walk into their HQ's inner yard. Choosing whose ground to cross becomes a real decision.\n487\t\n488\t**Brain:** a `BehaviorTree` for each soldier, ticked at 10 Hz, in priority order:\n489\t1. **On fire:** run in panic (`BurnPanic` clip), scream in gibberish, spread fire to the cells they cross, die in about 5 s.\n490\t2. **Fire near and upwind:** flee crosswind.\n491\t3. **Grenade or rocket nearby:** dodge.\n492\t4. **In combat:** take cover (site cover points, then nearest tree or prop within 12 m), fire bursts of 3 to 5, re-position every 4 to 8 s; one squad member flanks by `NavGrid.path`.\n493\t5. **Searching:** walk to the last known position, look about, give up after 20 s.\n494\t6. **Duty:** patrol, stand guard, sit by a fire, sleep at night.\n495\t\n496\tPathing uses a global `NavGrid` at 2 m (slope, water, buildings closed), budgeted per section 3; off the grid or far away they walk straight.\n497\t\n498\t**Shooting at you:** each round has an aim error `lerp(1.2°, 5°, dist/80) / TUNING.enemyAccuracy`, ×1.4 if you are moving fast. Damage per bullet 9. Reaction 0.45 s.\n499\t\n500\t**Vehicles:** patrol technicals follow road polylines with a PD steering controller, chase if alert, and their crews dismount at 25 m.\n501\t\n502\t**Barks** (gibberish voice plus a short subtitle, spatial): at least 15 per faction: spotted, lost you, grenade, jammed, fire, ally down. Examples in section 15.\n503\t\n504\t---\n505\t\n506\t## 11. Vehicles\n507\t\n508\tThree vehicles on `Vehicle` (tuning in section 3; truck heavier and slower): **pickup**, **technical** (pickup with MG on a pintle), **cargo truck** (also a tanker variant for M3). All have `model()` bodies, four wheel meshes posed by `wheelPose`, and suspension from the engine. One train: a kinematic body moved along the railway polyline, with flatcars.\n509\t\n510\t**Driving in first person:** eye at the driver's seat, your hands on a wheel that turns with steering, a dash, a small arrow on the dash pointing to your waypoint. R3/C toggles a chase camera (computed in your `step`, via `cam.override`). You can raise the map while driving, as you should: it's the most famous moment in this kind of game, and it's dangerous.\n511\t\n512\t**Getting in and out:** Use at a door. The player's capsule is disabled while seated and placed by the door on exit. Triangle/F swaps to the technical's gun; the truck rolls on with no driver, and that is your problem.\n513\t\n514\t**Damage:** 100 HP, from bullets, rockets, fire and collisions (over 8 m/s). Below 35: smoke, power × 0.6. Below 10: flames, explodes in 8 s unless you bail. At 0 and not on fire: stalled. **Repair:** stand at the bonnet, hold Use 3 s (wrench animation with sparks), back to 50 HP. The fixed truck coughs for a few seconds. Vehicles in M1 are scripted to break so everyone learns it.\n515\t\n516\tParking at a safehouse repairs fully overnight.\n517\t\n518\t---\n519\t\n520\t## 12. Buddies\n521\t\n522\tThree hired friends, each a named person with a real arc. All live in the bar at Mile Forty or at safehouses once you've met them.\n523\t\n524\t| | Ines Carvalho | Dov Halpern | Mags Oyelaran |\n525\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n526\t| Met | Freed from the cage, M2 | Tibor's shed, after M2; his plan in M4 | Clinic, after your first Mercy Run |\n527\t| Look | Flight cap, sunglasses, sand jacket | Bald, bandoliers, bad left hand | Braids, olive vest, medic's satchel with green cross |\n528\t| Perk | Rescues you by truck, from farther away | Gives 2 free charges per mission | +1 syrette at any safehouse; rescues you with 60 HP instead of 40 |\n529\t| Offers the alternate plan in | M3 | M4 | M5 |\n530\t| Voice | Mid, quick | Low, slow | High, warm, never stops |\n531\t\n532\t**Alternate plans.** On certain contracts the buddy calls (radio squelch, subtitles) with a better way, adding objectives and more risk, in exchange for bonus stones and +1 trust. You can accept or ignore them on the spot. If you take it, they fight beside you on that mission.\n533\t\n534\t**Rescue.** At HP 0 with a buddy available: the screen drops, and you are dragged backward in first person (low camera, sky, their boots, their gunfire) while they swear at you; then you are up at 40 HP (Mags 60) with them next to you, and the buddy is spent for 1 game day. 15% chance they take a wound and are out for 2 days. They remind you of it later.\n535\t\n536\t**Down.** A buddy fighting with you has 200 HP. At 0 they fall, wounded, for 40 s, marked by a floating pixel cross. At their side, a two-button prompt:\n537\t- `[Square/E] SYRETTE` (uses one; they're up at 50%, trust +1)\n538\t- `[Triangle/F] FINISH IT` (one shot, your sidearm's animation)\n539\t\n540\tIf you have no syrettes, only the second option is lit. If the 40 s run out, they die anyway. If they are burning, they ask you to finish it. M6 forces this moment at least once.\n541\t\n542\tA dead buddy stays dead: name scratched on the safehouse wall, their gun leaning under it, one Ledger line, and no more of their lines anywhere. The game must play on without any of them. Write their missions so the alternate plan just doesn't arrive.\n543\t\n544\t**At the end,** every surviving buddy comes to the Pass for the stones (section 14). Those with trust 3 or more first offer to split it, then draw anyway if you refuse.\n545\t\n546\t---\n547\t\n548\t## 13. Stones, safehouses, side content\n549\t\n550\t**Rough stones** are the money.\n551\t- Missions pay 5 to 25; cases hold 2 to 6.\n552\t- Total available in the demo is about 180; everything for sale costs about 130.\n553\t- Spent at **Tibor's** (a gun rack and a table).\n554\t\n555\t**Tibor's stock:** the guns in section 8 (buying one unlocks clean copies at every locker for free, forever), bottles, charges, and four upgrades:\n556\t- Cleaning kit (6 stones): wear × 0.6.\n557\t- Syrette pouch (5): carry 5.\n558\t- Ammo belt (5): +50% reserve.\n559\t- Vehicle kit (6): repair in 1.5 s.\n560\t\n561\t**The tracker.** Given in M4. D-pad Left/T raises it in your left hand: a small device with an LED and a beep that speeds up and turns green within 60 m of a stone case. Twelve cases are hidden around the Kettle (wrecks, hollow trees, under a dead man's truck, in guarded sheds).\n562\t\n563\t**Safehouses** (3):\n564\t- **Bed:** sleep to Dawn, Noon, Dusk or Midnight, and it saves.\n565\t- **Locker:** set your loadout.\n566\t- **Crate:** ammo and syrettes.\n567\t- A wall for names. Clear the guards first where there are any. Buddies wait here with offers.\n568\t\n569\t**Rail halts** (4): fast travel once visited, 1 stone, 1 game hour. It costs you Old Bakr's latest thought on a black screen with clacking wheels.\n570\t\n571\t**Trig points** (6): stone pillars on hilltops. Use one: a new note in Harrow's hand appears in your map's margin, and you can read it on the map. All six: he leaves you a clean `empire` at a locker. A note that says so.\n572\t\n573\t**Mercy Runs** (3, from Odile, plus M1): carry a crate to a marked place within 5 minutes. Pays 4 tablets. Fail and she says nothing, which is worse.\n574\t\n575\t**The Ledger.** Create/J in play, also in the pause menu, and at the end. One sheet, five big lines, at most (never a table):\n576\t- Hectares burned (burnt cells × 0.0025)\n577\t- People moved off their land\n578\t- Men you were paid to kill\n579\t- Friends lost\n580\t- Stones earned\n581\t\n582\tWritten as Harrow would write it.\n583\t\n584\t**Saving:** single slot, versioned JSON in `localStorage` (`src/core/save.js`), written on sleep and on mission complete, read through `ctx.input.send` so replays stay exact. Main menu's Continue loads it. Dev mode has Quick Save/Load.\n585\t\n586\t---\n587\t\n588\t## 14. Missions\n589\t\n590\t**Format** (`src/content/missions.js`), a sketch:\n591\t```js\n592\t{ id:'m3', title:'FUEL FOR THE PEACE', giver:'vance', requires:['m2'], pay:15, wind:{ dir:[-0.8,-0.6], speed:5 },\n593\t  brief:['vance:m3.brief.1','vance:m3.brief.2'],\n594\t  alt:{ buddy:'ines', call:'ines:m3.alt', bonus:5, steps:[ {do:'steal',tag:'tanker',text:'TAKE THE TANKER AT P3'} ] },\n595\t  steps:[ {do:'goto',site:'east-siding',r:140,text:'REACH THE SIDING'},\n596\t          {do:'destroy',tag:'fuel-tank',n:3,text:'BURN THE TANKS'},\n597\t          {do:'leave',site:'east-siding',r:220,text:'GET OUT'},\n598\t          {do:'report',to:'vance',text:'REPORT TO VANCE'} ],\n599\t  onDone:[ {burnStrip:'A'}, {ledger:{paid:15}} ] }\n600\t```\n601\t**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\n602\t\n603\tContracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four.\n604\t\n605\t| # | Title (giver) | Length, time | What happens | Teaches | Alternate plan | Consequence, pay |\n606\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n607\t| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\n608\t| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\n609\t| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\n610\t| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\n611\t| M4 | Seed Money (Ansa) | 7 min | Payroll convoy (2 technicals, a truck) crosses the Salt Pan on a loop. Stop it, take the case. It flies out when the truck blows: you get the tracker to find it in the salt | Vehicle combat, MG, tracker | Dov: plant his charges on the bridge, detonate as the convoy crosses | 20 stones (+5), tracker, Dov |\n612\t| M5 | The Water Question (Vance) | 7 min | Destroy the pump on the Mercy, because Three Wells \"feeds the Harvest\" | Charges, defending, moral cost | Mags: first open the bypass and hold the pump house for 60 s, so the cistern fills | Without alt: Three Wells empties, a line of people walks the road to the clinic, its huts go dark, Odile refuses tablets until you do a Mercy Run free. With alt: village stays, pay 10 instead of 20 |\n613\t| M6 | The Long Field (Ansa) | 9 min, forced night | Burn the Concord's crop and its ammo bunker. Your highest-trust buddy comes along. At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** | Night fire, buddy choice | The mission itself | Scar B, 25 stones, the Ledger's first hard line |\n614\t| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | Whoever's left calls in help | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\n615\t| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\n616\t| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\n617\t| End | The Pass | 3 to 4 min | Either walk to the Pass alone, or take the sheet to the column and hold behind them. Surviving buddies arrive (200 HP, real AI, last lines), with pursuit from both armies. Rain stops. The last grass is yours to light | Everything | - | Ending card, Ledger, credits, title. Continue returns to the last safehouse for free roam |\n618\t\n619\t**Story scars.** On completing M3, M6 and M7, call `burnStrip('A'|'B'|'C')` so the arc exists whatever the player actually burned: A from East Siding west to the Cut, C across the Cut, B from the Cut west through the Long Field to the Pass road. The player sees it first in M9.\n620\t\n621\t**Ending cards:**\n622\t- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\n623\t- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\n624\t\n625\t**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\n626\t\n627\t---\n628\t\n629\t## 15. Writing\n630\t\n631\t**Voice.** Weary, literary and exact. Short declarative sentences. Euphemism as cruelty. Gallows humour without a wink. Nobody explains the theme. Nobody is your friend without a price. People are tired, and they're smart. Think of a war correspondent who stopped filing years ago. Don't quote real authors, and don't imitate the source's lines.\n632\t\n633\tEach mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\n634\t\n635\tAll game text must be in the HUD font's character set. Subtitle lines stay under 60 characters, two lines at most: split long sentences across lines in sequence.\n636\t\n637\tUse these lines verbatim, and write the rest to match:\n638\t\n639\t- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\n640\t- **Odile:** *Three tablets. The fourth you pay for. I do not mean in stones.* / *I do not need you to be good. I need you to be on time.* / *Sixty-one beds. Forty blankets. You are the math.*\n641\t- **Vance:** *We do not burn villages. We conclude them.* / *The water question has been a great sorrow to this office.* / *Your invoice will be honoured, regrettably.*\n642\t- **Ansa:** *You said less people. Fewer. Fewer people. It will matter by the end of the month.* / *Burn the field. A hungry man learns to read the wind.*\n643\t- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\n644\t- **Ines:** *I flew for both of them. Neither paid. Get in.* / *You owe me a truck. You owe me several trucks.*\n645\t- **Dov:** *Two fingers I left in this country. I came back to see what they are doing.* / *A man asked me to mine his own road, so he would know where it was safe. He was right for a week.*\n646\t- **Mags:** *Hold still. No, you can't feel that. No, that's normal. Hold still.* / *Not today. Today you owe me money.*\n647\t- **A burning buddy:** *Don't let it be the fire. Please. Not the fire.*\n648\t- **Barks:** *There! In the grass!* / *Who lit that?* / *It's stuck! It's stuck again!* / *Leave him, he's already gone.*\n649\t- **Harrow's margin notes,** one per trig point, in order:\n650\t  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\n651\t  2. *I drew the river where the Company wanted it. The river was slow to comply, but it came round.*\n652\t  3. *Both armies buy from me. The Concord pays on time. The Harvest pays in grain and tears. I have eaten better on the tears.*\n653\t  4. *You will have noticed that you follow roads. I drew those too.*\n654\t  5. *Grass is the only honest border. It goes where the wind tells it, and it keeps a record.*\n655\t  6. *By now you have burned what I marked. Look at it from the ridge. Tell me that is not a line.*\n656\t- **Harrow, M9:** *You are late. I said you would be. Sit down, it won't take long, neither of us has long.* / *I drew the lines that started this. I would like to draw one more.* / *You have been drawing for me. Look at it.* / *Burned grass cannot burn twice. It is the only safe road in the country, and you built it for wages.*\n657\t- **Load-screen epigraphs** (*from Harrow's field notes*): write 12 in the same voice.\n658\t\n659\t---\n660\t\n661\t## 16. UI and UX\n662\t\n663\t**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\n664\t\n665\t**Layout rules:**\n666\t- Safe area 24 px horizontal, 14 px vertical.\n667\t- Menu items at scale 2; the smallest text anywhere is scale 1 (subtitles, prompts).\n668\t- At most 6 items on a screen, one idea per screen.\n669\t- No tables, no scroll lists, no web-style data screens. Long content is paged.\n670\t- A focused item has a full-width bar in `orange` and a small marker. Move and confirm sounds.\n671\t- Pause menu and title only: all other screens are diegetic or overlays with the world visible behind.\n672\t\n673\t**HUD in play is minimal** and hides 6 s after it last changed:\n674\t- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\n675\t- Ammo and the gun's condition icon bottom-right.\n676\t- A dot reticle (hidden while scoped; the scope has its own black mask).\n677\t- Prompts centre-bottom. Subtitles above them with the speaker's name in a colour.\n678\t- Mission step at the top for 5 s when it changes.\n679\t\n680\t**Controls** (`src/core/actions.js`):\n681\t\n682\t| Action | DualSense | Xbox glyph | Keyboard and mouse |\n683\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n684\t| Move / look | L stick / R stick | same | WASD / mouse |\n685\t| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\n686\t| Use (when a prompt shows), else reload | Square | X | E / R |\n687\t| Jump | Cross | A | Space |\n688\t| Crouch | Circle | B | C or Ctrl |\n689\t| Sprint | L3 | LS | Left Shift |\n690\t| Melee | R3 | RS | F |\n691\t| Next weapon | Triangle | Y | Wheel, or 1-4 |\n692\t| Throw / plant | R1 | RB | G |\n693\t| Syrette, surgery | L1 | LB | Q |\n694\t| Map up / down | D-pad Up | D-pad Up | M or Tab |\n695\t| Tablet | D-pad Down | D-pad Down | H |\n696\t| Tracker | D-pad Left | D-pad Left | T |\n697\t| Monocular (hold) | D-pad Right | D-pad Right | V |\n698\t| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\n699\t| Ledger | Create | View | J |\n700\t| **Driving:** gas / brake-reverse / steer | R2 / L2 / L stick | RT / LT / L stick | W / S / A-D |\n701\t| Handbrake | Cross | A | Space |\n702\t| Get out / repair | Square | X | E |\n703\t| Swap to gun | Triangle | Y | F |\n704\t| Chase camera | R3 | RS | C |\n705\t\n706\tUse `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')` etc. Analog triggers: each frame, read `navigator.getGamepads()` buttons 6 and 7 `value` and `input.send({ tr:[l2, r2] })` when changed, so recordings keep it, and use it for throttle and brake. Rumble: `pad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', {...})`, guarded, Settings toggle.\n707\t\n708\t**Glyphs.** Prompts follow the input used last:\n709\t- `device` flips to `kbm` on keydown, mouse button or real mouse movement, and to `pad` on any `Pad*` code or a stick past 0.35.\n710\t- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; a key cap drawn around any letter; LMB, RMB, MMB, wheel.\n711\t- Settings has **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**, default PlayStation.\n712\t- `game.state().prompts` lists what's on screen, so tests can check it.\n713\t\n714\t**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back.\n715\t\n716\t**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\n717\t- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\n718\t- Baked at start: contour lines every 8 m on sand paper, river, roads, rail, labels in your own 5×7 `pixfont.js`.\n719\t- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\n720\t- Raise and lower takes 0.4 s with paper sound. **The world never stops.** You can walk and drive with it up. While it's up, the look input moves the map cursor.\n721\t- Square/LMB on a marker sets the waypoint; Triangle or wheel toggles a closer zoom.\n722\t- It works at night because the paper uses a dim lit toon plus a small hand torch `lights.request` following the view group.\n723\t\n724\t**Screens:**\n725\t- **Loading:** the engine's, then a black screen with one Harrow epigraph.\n726\t- **Title:** live 3D scene (dusk, fixed slow camera over burning grass on the Long Field, music), the title large (scale 4, or 3 if it won't fit), the latest input's *Press [glyph]*. Then the main menu.\n727\t- **Main menu:** Continue (when a save exists), New Game, Cash Run, Settings, About and Credits.\n728\t- **Pause** (`timeScale = 0`): Resume, Ledger, Settings, Dev Mode, About and Credits, Quit to Title. In a hub session: Resume and Settings only.\n729\t- **Settings:** Sound (Music slider **default 10%**, Effects, Voices), Controls (Look sensitivity for pad, for mouse; Invert Y; Aim assist; Rumble; Glyphs), Picture (Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in `localStorage`; `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's own panel.\n730\t- **Dialogue:** the camera holds on the speaker; subtitles; two big buttons at most.\n731\t- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\n732\t- **Locker:** one row per slot, left/right picks.\n733\t- **Bed:** Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, Leave.\n734\t- **Ledger:** section 13.\n735\t- **Game Over, Ending card, Credits.**\n736\t- **About and Credits:** paged, see section 27.\n737\t\n738\t**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this screen. A key press or pad connecting clears the gate and shows the normal title.\n739\t\n740\t---\n741\t\n742\t## 17. Dev mode\n743\t\n744\tPause menu → **Dev Mode** (hidden in a hub session). An overlay with tabs (L1/R1 or Q/E), world visible behind, playing or frozen by a toggle.\n745\t\n746\t| Tab | Contents |\n747\t| --- | --- |\n748\t| Cheats | God mode, infinite ammo, no jams, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip fly |\n749\t| Teleport | Every site, every post, every case, the crosshair point |\n750\t| Spawn | Squad of each faction, pickup, technical, truck, a stone case, a buddy |\n751\t| World | Hour slider, wind direction and speed sliders, weather (clear, dust, storm), ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, sleep +6 h |\n752\t| Mission | Start any mission, complete current step, set story flags, give stones, tablets, syrettes, all guns; break gun; force jam; force fever; down a buddy |\n753\t| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), **Reset to Defaults** for all, Square/R resets one |\n754\t| Debug | Fire-grid overlay, nav overlay, AI state text over heads, counts (actors, burning cells, draw info from `engine.state()`), engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug`), free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset:'free' })`, restored after; re-install `step` in `onCameraChange`), crosshair coordinates for placing things in `src/content/`, Quick Save/Load, show `status()` |\n755\t\n756\t**Balance sliders** (left/right steps, hold accelerates, mouse drags). Defaults in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`:\n757\t\n758\t| Slider | Default | Range |\n759\t| --- | --- | --- |\n760\t| `playerSpeed` multiplier | 1 | 0.5-2 |\n761\t| `playerDamageTaken` multiplier | 1 | 0-3 |\n762\t| `weaponDamage` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n763\t| `enemyHealth` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n764\t| `enemyAccuracy` | 1 | 0.25-3 |\n765\t| `enemyVision` (m) | 90 | 20-200 |\n766\t| `enemyReaction` (s) | 0.45 | 0.1-2 |\n767\t| `wearRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n768\t| `jamRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n769\t| `fireSpread` | 1 | 0-3 |\n770\t| `fireDamage` (HP/s) | 8 | 0-30 |\n771\t| `windEffect` | 1 | 0-3 |\n772\t| `feverMinutes` | 12 | 2-40 |\n773\t| `vehicleTopSpeed` (m/s) | 26 | 10-45 |\n774\t| `vehicleToughness` | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n775\t| `stonesReward` multiplier | 1 | 0-5 |\n776\t| `buddyWoundChance` | 0.15 | 0-1 |\n777\t| `dayMinutes` | 30 | 2-120 |\n778\t| `postRemanHours` | 24 | 1-96 |\n779\t| `regrowHours` | 48 | 1-200 |\n780\t\n781\tA test sets every slider, checks the system responds, presses Reset, and checks every value equals its default.\n782\t\n783\t---\n784\t\n785\t## 18. Attract mode\n786\t\n787\tAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title or any main-menu screen**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). It's a director with a list of beats, using the real game with `cam.override`, god mode, infinite ammo and bot input through the same action layer. It cheats freely: teleports, spawns, sets the hour and wind. A `save.disabled` flag stops it touching saves.\n788\t\n789\tBeats (10 to 14 s each, joined by `engine.screen.cover('dither')` and `reveal`), to show as much as possible:\n790\t1. Dusk, driving a technical down the road, first person, raising the map at the wheel.\n791\t2. Rolling into a checkpoint, gunfight, the gun jams, slap and rack.\n792\t3. Flare into dry grass, the wind takes it, soldiers run burning.\n793\t4. Night, the Long Field in flames, chase camera past it.\n794\t5. Fever: the view swims, tablet to mouth.\n795\t6. Field surgery with pliers.\n796\t7. Scoped shot from a ridge at noon.\n797\t8. Dragged out by a buddy; syrette or finish it.\n798\t9. Tracker beeping to a case in a burnt wreck."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"de4c9362-c73e-48a4-ac53-e8b357aed696","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:08:19.354Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work/PLAN.md","content":"  Keyed with the hands rig (section 21), with pixel blood, sound and a grunt. These are a highlight, so make them good.\n- **Burning:** catching fire does 8 HP/s plus orange flames at the screen edge until you leave fuel for 2 s or reach water.\n- **Down at 0:** if a buddy is available, a rescue scene plays (section 12). Otherwise: *YOU DIED IN THE SORREL. THE PAPERWORK WILL TAKE LONGER.* Then Continue (last save) or Title.\n\n**Blackwater fever.** The source's malaria idea, with a clock you can feel.\n- `TUNING.feverMinutes` (default 12) ± 2 between attacks; the interval shrinks by 1 minute after each act. First attack scripted in M0.\n- **Onset:** view sways, `chromatic.spread` climbs to 4, saturation falls, warmth up, heartbeat, a line in the subtitle band (*THE FEVER.* or variants), and the prompt `[glyph] TABLET`.\n- **With a tablet** (D-pad Down/H, hold 1 s, hand-to-mouth animation): clears over 5 s.\n- **Ignored for 25 s, or no tablets:** vision narrows, you fall, and you wake at the nearest safehouse or the clinic hours later, with 20% of your stones gone. Buddy if available: they carry you and complain.\n- **Supply:** 3 after M1; Mercy Runs pay 4 each (section 13). Tablets can't be bought with stones. That is the point: Odile wants your time.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Soldiers and AI\n\n**Bodies:** the soldier model in faction palettes (several `skin` values and hat variants), a rifle parented to `HandR`, a `CharacterController` capsule (speed from role), `physics.tag(collider, 'npc')` and a `Map` from collider handle to actor. Clips are in section 21.\n\n**Roles:** rifle (most), mg (slower, heavier burst), sniper (towers, long range), rocket (rare), driver.\n\n**Perception.**\n- Vision cone 120°, range `TUNING.enemyVision` (90 m) × stance (crouch 0.55, in tall grass 0.6) × light (night 0.45, doubled if you are lit by fire or muzzle flash).\n- LOS by `physics.castRay` to head and chest.\n- A suspicion meter fills over about 1.5 s by distance. States: `idle → suspicious → alert → searching → idle`.\n- Hearing: gunshot radius per weapon (rifle 120 m), sprint 40 m, run 25 m.\n- Squad members share the last known position.\n- Close by, a small pixel `?` or `!` floats over the head (HUD text projected through the camera). That is the only detection UI.\n\n**Hostility.** Everyone outside Mile Forty shoots you on sight, with one exception: **while you hold a contract from a faction, you carry its pass**, and its soldiers leave you alone unless you fire near them or walk into their HQ's inner yard. Choosing whose ground to cross becomes a real decision.\n\n**Brain:** a `BehaviorTree` for each soldier, ticked at 10 Hz, in priority order:\n1. **On fire:** run in panic (`BurnPanic` clip), scream in gibberish, spread fire to the cells they cross, die in about 5 s.\n2. **Fire near and upwind:** flee crosswind.\n3. **Grenade or rocket nearby:** dodge.\n4. **In combat:** take cover (site cover points, then nearest tree or prop within 12 m), fire bursts of 3 to 5, re-position every 4 to 8 s; one squad member flanks by `NavGrid.path`.\n5. **Searching:** walk to the last known position, look about, give up after 20 s.\n6. **Duty:** patrol, stand guard, sit by a fire, sleep at night.\n\nPathing uses a global `NavGrid` at 2 m (slope, water, buildings closed), budgeted per section 3; off the grid or far away they walk straight.\n\n**Shooting at you:** each round has an aim error `lerp(1.2°, 5°, dist/80) / TUNING.enemyAccuracy`, ×1.4 if you are moving fast. Damage per bullet 9. Reaction 0.45 s.\n\n**Vehicles:** patrol technicals follow road polylines with a PD steering controller, chase if alert, and their crews dismount at 25 m.\n\n**Barks** (gibberish voice plus a short subtitle, spatial): at least 15 per faction: spotted, lost you, grenade, jammed, fire, ally down. Examples in section 15.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Vehicles\n\nThree vehicles on `Vehicle` (tuning in section 3; truck heavier and slower): **pickup**, **technical** (pickup with MG on a pintle), **cargo truck** (also a tanker variant for M3). All have `model()` bodies, four wheel meshes posed by `wheelPose`, and suspension from the engine. One train: a kinematic body moved along the railway polyline, with flatcars.\n\n**Driving in first person:** eye at the driver's seat, your hands on a wheel that turns with steering, a dash, a small arrow on the dash pointing to your waypoint. R3/C toggles a chase camera (computed in your `step`, via `cam.override`). You can raise the map while driving, as you should: it's the most famous moment in this kind of game, and it's dangerous.\n\n**Getting in and out:** Use at a door. The player's capsule is disabled while seated and placed by the door on exit. Triangle/F swaps to the technical's gun; the truck rolls on with no driver, and that is your problem.\n\n**Damage:** 100 HP, from bullets, rockets, fire and collisions (over 8 m/s). Below 35: smoke, power × 0.6. Below 10: flames, explodes in 8 s unless you bail. At 0 and not on fire: stalled. **Repair:** stand at the bonnet, hold Use 3 s (wrench animation with sparks), back to 50 HP. The fixed truck coughs for a few seconds. Vehicles in M1 are scripted to break so everyone learns it.\n\nParking at a safehouse repairs fully overnight.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Buddies\n\nThree hired friends, each a named person with a real arc. All live in the bar at Mile Forty or at safehouses once you've met them.\n\n| | Ines Carvalho | Dov Halpern | Mags Oyelaran |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Met | Freed from the cage, M2 | Tibor's shed, after M2; his plan in M4 | Clinic, after your first Mercy Run |\n| Look | Flight cap, sunglasses, sand jacket | Bald, bandoliers, bad left hand | Braids, olive vest, medic's satchel with green cross |\n| Perk | Rescues you by truck, from farther away | Gives 2 free charges per mission | +1 syrette at any safehouse; rescues you with 60 HP instead of 40 |\n| Offers the alternate plan in | M3 | M4 | M5 |\n| Voice | Mid, quick | Low, slow | High, warm, never stops |\n\n**Alternate plans.** On certain contracts the buddy calls (radio squelch, subtitles) with a better way, adding objectives and more risk, in exchange for bonus stones and +1 trust. You can accept or ignore them on the spot. If you take it, they fight beside you on that mission.\n\n**Rescue.** At HP 0 with a buddy available: the screen drops, and you are dragged backward in first person (low camera, sky, their boots, their gunfire) while they swear at you; then you are up at 40 HP (Mags 60) with them next to you, and the buddy is spent for 1 game day. 15% chance they take a wound and are out for 2 days. They remind you of it later.\n\n**Down.** A buddy fighting with you has 200 HP. At 0 they fall, wounded, for 40 s, marked by a floating pixel cross. At their side, a two-button prompt:\n- `[Square/E] SYRETTE` (uses one; they're up at 50%, trust +1)\n- `[Triangle/F] FINISH IT` (one shot, your sidearm's animation)\n\nIf you have no syrettes, only the second option is lit. If the 40 s run out, they die anyway. If they are burning, they ask you to finish it. M6 forces this moment at least once.\n\nA dead buddy stays dead: name scratched on the safehouse wall, their gun leaning under it, one Ledger line, and no more of their lines anywhere. The game must play on without any of them. Write their missions so the alternate plan just doesn't arrive.\n\n**At the end,** every surviving buddy comes to the Pass for the stones (section 14). Those with trust 3 or more first offer to split it, then draw anyway if you refuse.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Stones, safehouses, side content\n\n**Rough stones** are the money.\n- Missions pay 5 to 25; cases hold 2 to 6.\n- Total available in the demo is about 180; everything for sale costs about 130.\n- Spent at **Tibor's** (a gun rack and a table).\n\n**Tibor's stock:** the guns in section 8 (buying one unlocks clean copies at every locker for free, forever), bottles, charges, and four upgrades:\n- Cleaning kit (6 stones): wear × 0.6.\n- Syrette pouch (5): carry 5.\n- Ammo belt (5): +50% reserve.\n- Vehicle kit (6): repair in 1.5 s.\n\n**The tracker.** Given in M4. D-pad Left/T raises it in your left hand: a small device with an LED and a beep that speeds up and turns green within 60 m of a stone case. Twelve cases are hidden around the Kettle (wrecks, hollow trees, under a dead man's truck, in guarded sheds).\n\n**Safehouses** (3):\n- **Bed:** sleep to Dawn, Noon, Dusk or Midnight, and it saves.\n- **Locker:** set your loadout.\n- **Crate:** ammo and syrettes.\n- A wall for names. Clear the guards first where there are any. Buddies wait here with offers.\n\n**Rail halts** (4): fast travel once visited, 1 stone, 1 game hour. It costs you Old Bakr's latest thought on a black screen with clacking wheels.\n\n**Trig points** (6): stone pillars on hilltops. Use one: a new note in Harrow's hand appears in your map's margin, and you can read it on the map. All six: he leaves you a clean `empire` at a locker. A note that says so.\n\n**Mercy Runs** (3, from Odile, plus M1): carry a crate to a marked place within 5 minutes. Pays 4 tablets. Fail and she says nothing, which is worse.\n\n**The Ledger.** Create/J in play, also in the pause menu, and at the end. One sheet, five big lines, at most (never a table):\n- Hectares burned (burnt cells × 0.0025)\n- People moved off their land\n- Men you were paid to kill\n- Friends lost\n- Stones earned\n\nWritten as Harrow would write it.\n\n**Saving:** single slot, versioned JSON in `localStorage` (`src/core/save.js`), written on sleep and on mission complete, read through `ctx.input.send` so replays stay exact. Main menu's Continue loads it. Dev mode has Quick Save/Load.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Missions\n\n**Format** (`src/content/missions.js`), a sketch:\n```js\n{ id:'m3', title:'FUEL FOR THE PEACE', giver:'vance', requires:['m2'], pay:15, wind:{ dir:[-0.8,-0.6], speed:5 },\n  brief:['vance:m3.brief.1','vance:m3.brief.2'],\n  alt:{ buddy:'ines', call:'ines:m3.alt', bonus:5, steps:[ {do:'steal',tag:'tanker',text:'TAKE THE TANKER AT P3'} ] },\n  steps:[ {do:'goto',site:'east-siding',r:140,text:'REACH THE SIDING'},\n          {do:'destroy',tag:'fuel-tank',n:3,text:'BURN THE TANKS'},\n          {do:'leave',site:'east-siding',r:220,text:'GET OUT'},\n          {do:'report',to:'vance',text:'REPORT TO VANCE'} ],\n  onDone:[ {burnStrip:'A'}, {ledger:{paid:15}} ] }\n```\n**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\n\nContracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four.\n\n| # | Title (giver) | Length, time | What happens | Teaches | Alternate plan | Consequence, pay |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\n| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\n| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\n| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\n| M4 | Seed Money (Ansa) | 7 min | Payroll convoy (2 technicals, a truck) crosses the Salt Pan on a loop. Stop it, take the case. It flies out when the truck blows: you get the tracker to find it in the salt | Vehicle combat, MG, tracker | Dov: plant his charges on the bridge, detonate as the convoy crosses | 20 stones (+5), tracker, Dov |\n| M5 | The Water Question (Vance) | 7 min | Destroy the pump on the Mercy, because Three Wells \"feeds the Harvest\" | Charges, defending, moral cost | Mags: first open the bypass and hold the pump house for 60 s, so the cistern fills | Without alt: Three Wells empties, a line of people walks the road to the clinic, its huts go dark, Odile refuses tablets until you do a Mercy Run free. With alt: village stays, pay 10 instead of 20 |\n| M6 | The Long Field (Ansa) | 9 min, forced night | Burn the Concord's crop and its ammo bunker. Your highest-trust buddy comes along. At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** | Night fire, buddy choice | The mission itself | Scar B, 25 stones, the Ledger's first hard line |\n| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | Whoever's left calls in help | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\n| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\n| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\n| End | The Pass | 3 to 4 min | Either walk to the Pass alone, or take the sheet to the column and hold behind them. Surviving buddies arrive (200 HP, real AI, last lines), with pursuit from both armies. Rain stops. The last grass is yours to light | Everything | - | Ending card, Ledger, credits, title. Continue returns to the last safehouse for free roam |\n\n**Story scars.** On completing M3, M6 and M7, call `burnStrip('A'|'B'|'C')` so the arc exists whatever the player actually burned: A from East Siding west to the Cut, C across the Cut, B from the Cut west through the Long Field to the Pass road. The player sees it first in M9.\n\n**Ending cards:**\n- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\n- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\n\n**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Writing\n\n**Voice.** Weary, literary and exact. Short declarative sentences. Euphemism as cruelty. Gallows humour without a wink. Nobody explains the theme. Nobody is your friend without a price. People are tired, and they're smart. Think of a war correspondent who stopped filing years ago. Don't quote real authors, and don't imitate the source's lines.\n\nEach mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\n\nAll game text must be in the HUD font's character set. Subtitle lines stay under 60 characters, two lines at most: split long sentences across lines in sequence.\n\nUse these lines verbatim, and write the rest to match:\n\n- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\n- **Odile:** *Three tablets. The fourth you pay for. I do not mean in stones.* / *I do not need you to be good. I need you to be on time.* / *Sixty-one beds. Forty blankets. You are the math.*\n- **Vance:** *We do not burn villages. We conclude them.* / *The water question has been a great sorrow to this office.* / *Your invoice will be honoured, regrettably.*\n- **Ansa:** *You said less people. Fewer. Fewer people. It will matter by the end of the month.* / *Burn the field. A hungry man learns to read the wind.*\n- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\n- **Ines:** *I flew for both of them. Neither paid. Get in.* / *You owe me a truck. You owe me several trucks.*\n- **Dov:** *Two fingers I left in this country. I came back to see what they are doing.* / *A man asked me to mine his own road, so he would know where it was safe. He was right for a week.*\n- **Mags:** *Hold still. No, you can't feel that. No, that's normal. Hold still.* / *Not today. Today you owe me money.*\n- **A burning buddy:** *Don't let it be the fire. Please. Not the fire.*\n- **Barks:** *There! In the grass!* / *Who lit that?* / *It's stuck! It's stuck again!* / *Leave him, he's already gone.*\n- **Harrow's margin notes,** one per trig point, in order:\n  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\n  2. *I drew the river where the Company wanted it. The river was slow to comply, but it came round.*\n  3. *Both armies buy from me. The Concord pays on time. The Harvest pays in grain and tears. I have eaten better on the tears.*\n  4. *You will have noticed that you follow roads. I drew those too.*\n  5. *Grass is the only honest border. It goes where the wind tells it, and it keeps a record.*\n  6. *By now you have burned what I marked. Look at it from the ridge. Tell me that is not a line.*\n- **Harrow, M9:** *You are late. I said you would be. Sit down, it won't take long, neither of us has long.* / *I drew the lines that started this. I would like to draw one more.* / *You have been drawing for me. Look at it.* / *Burned grass cannot burn twice. It is the only safe road in the country, and you built it for wages.*\n- **Load-screen epigraphs** (*from Harrow's field notes*): write 12 in the same voice.\n\n---\n\n## 16. UI and UX\n\n**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\n\n**Layout rules:**\n- Safe area 24 px horizontal, 14 px vertical.\n- Menu items at scale 2; the smallest text anywhere is scale 1 (subtitles, prompts).\n- At most 6 items on a screen, one idea per screen.\n- No tables, no scroll lists, no web-style data screens. Long content is paged.\n- A focused item has a full-width bar in `orange` and a small marker. Move and confirm sounds.\n- Pause menu and title only: all other screens are diegetic or overlays with the world visible behind.\n\n**HUD in play is minimal** and hides 6 s after it last changed:\n- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\n- Ammo and the gun's condition icon bottom-right.\n- A dot reticle (hidden while scoped; the scope has its own black mask).\n- Prompts centre-bottom. Subtitles above them with the speaker's name in a colour.\n- Mission step at the top for 5 s when it changes.\n\n**Controls** (`src/core/actions.js`):\n\n| Action | DualSense | Xbox glyph | Keyboard and mouse |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Move / look | L stick / R stick | same | WASD / mouse |\n| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\n| Use (when a prompt shows), else reload | Square | X | E / R |\n| Jump | Cross | A | Space |\n| Crouch | Circle | B | C or Ctrl |\n| Sprint | L3 | LS | Left Shift |\n| Melee | R3 | RS | F |\n| Next weapon | Triangle | Y | Wheel, or 1-4 |\n| Throw / plant | R1 | RB | G |\n| Syrette, surgery | L1 | LB | Q |\n| Map up / down | D-pad Up | D-pad Up | M or Tab |\n| Tablet | D-pad Down | D-pad Down | H |\n| Tracker | D-pad Left | D-pad Left | T |\n| Monocular (hold) | D-pad Right | D-pad Right | V |\n| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\n| Ledger | Create | View | J |\n| **Driving:** gas / brake-reverse / steer | R2 / L2 / L stick | RT / LT / L stick | W / S / A-D |\n| Handbrake | Cross | A | Space |\n| Get out / repair | Square | X | E |\n| Swap to gun | Triangle | Y | F |\n| Chase camera | R3 | RS | C |\n\nUse `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')` etc. Analog triggers: each frame, read `navigator.getGamepads()` buttons 6 and 7 `value` and `input.send({ tr:[l2, r2] })` when changed, so recordings keep it, and use it for throttle and brake. Rumble: `pad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', {...})`, guarded, Settings toggle.\n\n**Glyphs.** Prompts follow the input used last:\n- `device` flips to `kbm` on keydown, mouse button or real mouse movement, and to `pad` on any `Pad*` code or a stick past 0.35.\n- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; a key cap drawn around any letter; LMB, RMB, MMB, wheel.\n- Settings has **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**, default PlayStation.\n- `game.state().prompts` lists what's on screen, so tests can check it.\n\n**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back.\n\n**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\n- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\n- Baked at start: contour lines every 8 m on sand paper, river, roads, rail, labels in your own 5×7 `pixfont.js`.\n- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\n- Raise and lower takes 0.4 s with paper sound. **The world never stops.** You can walk and drive with it up. While it's up, the look input moves the map cursor.\n- Square/LMB on a marker sets the waypoint; Triangle or wheel toggles a closer zoom.\n- It works at night because the paper uses a dim lit toon plus a small hand torch `lights.request` following the view group.\n\n**Screens:**\n- **Loading:** the engine's, then a black screen with one Harrow epigraph.\n- **Title:** live 3D scene (dusk, fixed slow camera over burning grass on the Long Field, music), the title large (scale 4, or 3 if it won't fit), the latest input's *Press [glyph]*. Then the main menu.\n- **Main menu:** Continue (when a save exists), New Game, Cash Run, Settings, About and Credits.\n- **Pause** (`timeScale = 0`): Resume, Ledger, Settings, Dev Mode, About and Credits, Quit to Title. In a hub session: Resume and Settings only.\n- **Settings:** Sound (Music slider **default 10%**, Effects, Voices), Controls (Look sensitivity for pad, for mouse; Invert Y; Aim assist; Rumble; Glyphs), Picture (Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in `localStorage`; `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's own panel.\n- **Dialogue:** the camera holds on the speaker; subtitles; two big buttons at most.\n- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\n- **Locker:** one row per slot, left/right picks.\n- **Bed:** Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, Leave.\n- **Ledger:** section 13.\n- **Game Over, Ending card, Credits.**\n- **About and Credits:** paged, see section 27.\n\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this screen. A key press or pad connecting clears the gate and shows the normal title.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Dev mode\n\nPause menu → **Dev Mode** (hidden in a hub session). An overlay with tabs (L1/R1 or Q/E), world visible behind, playing or frozen by a toggle.\n\n| Tab | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| Cheats | God mode, infinite ammo, no jams, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip fly |\n| Teleport | Every site, every post, every case, the crosshair point |\n| Spawn | Squad of each faction, pickup, technical, truck, a stone case, a buddy |\n| World | Hour slider, wind direction and speed sliders, weather (clear, dust, storm), ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, sleep +6 h |\n| Mission | Start any mission, complete current step, set story flags, give stones, tablets, syrettes, all guns; break gun; force jam; force fever; down a buddy |\n| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), **Reset to Defaults** for all, Square/R resets one |\n| Debug | Fire-grid overlay, nav overlay, AI state text over heads, counts (actors, burning cells, draw info from `engine.state()`), engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug`), free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset:'free' })`, restored after; re-install `step` in `onCameraChange`), crosshair coordinates for placing things in `src/content/`, Quick Save/Load, show `status()` |\n\n**Balance sliders** (left/right steps, hold accelerates, mouse drags). Defaults in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`:\n\n| Slider | Default | Range |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `playerSpeed` multiplier | 1 | 0.5-2 |\n| `playerDamageTaken` multiplier | 1 | 0-3 |\n| `weaponDamage` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n| `enemyHealth` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n| `enemyAccuracy` | 1 | 0.25-3 |\n| `enemyVision` (m) | 90 | 20-200 |\n| `enemyReaction` (s) | 0.45 | 0.1-2 |\n| `wearRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n| `jamRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n| `fireSpread` | 1 | 0-3 |\n| `fireDamage` (HP/s) | 8 | 0-30 |\n| `windEffect` | 1 | 0-3 |\n| `feverMinutes` | 12 | 2-40 |\n| `vehicleTopSpeed` (m/s) | 26 | 10-45 |\n| `vehicleToughness` | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n| `stonesReward` multiplier | 1 | 0-5 |\n| `buddyWoundChance` | 0.15 | 0-1 |\n| `dayMinutes` | 30 | 2-120 |\n| `postRemanHours` | 24 | 1-96 |\n| `regrowHours` | 48 | 1-200 |\n\nA test sets every slider, checks the system responds, presses Reset, and checks every value equals its default.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title or any main-menu screen**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). It's a director with a list of beats, using the real game with `cam.override`, god mode, infinite ammo and bot input through the same action layer. It cheats freely: teleports, spawns, sets the hour and wind. A `save.disabled` flag stops it touching saves.\n\nBeats (10 to 14 s each, joined by `engine.screen.cover('dither')` and `reveal`), to show as much as possible:\n1. Dusk, driving a technical down the road, first person, raising the map at the wheel.\n2. Rolling into a checkpoint, gunfight, the gun jams, slap and rack.\n3. Flare into dry grass, the wind takes it, soldiers run burning.\n4. Night, the Long Field in flames, chase camera past it.\n5. Fever: the view swims, tablet to mouth.\n6. Field surgery with pliers.\n7. Scoped shot from a ridge at noon.\n8. Dragged out by a buddy; syrette or finish it.\n9. Tracker beeping to a case in a burnt wreck.","numLines":340,"startLine":459,"totalLines":1127}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017eyTHubaEsCJK9Vwy2iYMJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
