{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJM38pgt8rezginQqLzafw","type":"tool_result","content":"179-    debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption;\n180-    /**\n181-     * The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate,\n182-     * sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true:\n183-     * 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for none: open the\n184-     * panel from your own menu (`engine.settings.open()`). `key`: where they are saved\n185-     * (localStorage `pixel-engine:settings:<key>`; default the first game's name), false: nowhere.\n186-     */\n187:    settings?: {\n### type DebugKeysOption\n\n```ts\ntype DebugKeysOption = DebugKeyChanges | boolean\n```\n\n`EngineOptions.debugKeys`. Left out, the hotkeys come with the debug panel: on in the dev\nserver and with `?debug=1`, off otherwise. `true` turns the defaults on always and `false` off\nalways. An object rebinds (a key code, a list of codes) or disables (`null` / `[]`) single\nactions, and the keys still come with the debug panel.\n\n  debugKeys: { resolution: 'F2', mute: null }   // with the panel: R freed for the game, no mute key\n\n52 70","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"b8440e3c-cb48-40eb-9ab4-96218d98b183","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:25.069Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"179-    debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption;\n180-    /**\n181-     * The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate,\n182-     * sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true:\n183-     * 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for none: open the\n184-     * panel from your own menu (`engine.settings.open()`). `key`: where they are saved\n185-     * (localStorage `pixel-engine:settings:<key>`; default the first game's name), false: nowhere.\n186-     */\n187:    settings?: {\n### type DebugKeysOption\n\n```ts\ntype DebugKeysOption = DebugKeyChanges | boolean\n```\n\n`EngineOptions.debugKeys`. Left out, the hotkeys come with the debug panel: on in the dev\nserver and with `?debug=1`, off otherwise. `true` turns the defaults on always and `false` off\nalways. An object rebinds (a key code, a list of codes) or disables (`null` / `[]`) single\nactions, and the keys still come with the debug panel.\n\n  debugKeys: { resolution: 'F2', mute: null }   // with the panel: R freed for the game, no mute key\n\n52 70","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GJM38pgt8rezginQqLzafw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
