{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCnhKhAr3iSmca7gib8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm applying the fixes for the traps found in the final read-through, such as Ctrl meaning Ctrl+W closes the tab, and then writing the exit interview.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4804,"cache_read_input_tokens":514018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4804},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"0f6c8973-3730-47ea-9612-65cab8ed58d3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:28.727Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCnh2aktGdKoomoLx2P","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCnhKhAr3iSmca7gib8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BsYebGs3V7MVfQEhy1NpzA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"W=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work; cat > $W/.scratch/spike/patch2.py <<'PY'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    if a not in s: raise SystemExit('NOT FOUND: '+a[:90])\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n\n# browser keyboard traps\nrep(\"| Crouch | Circle | B | C or Ctrl |\",\"| Crouch | Circle | B | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab) |\")\nrep(\"| Walk (stick partly tilted or Alt held) | 3.6 | Quiet |\",\"| Walk (stick partly tilted; Caps Lock toggles it on keyboard, never Alt, since Alt+D jumps to the address bar) | 3.6 | Quiet |\")\nrep(\"| Sprint (hold L3/Shift while moving forward) | 7.4 |\",\"| Sprint (click L3 or hold Shift while moving forward) | 7.4 |\")\nrep(\"| Sprint | L3 | LS | Left Shift |\",\"| Sprint | L3 (click) | LS | Left Shift |\")\n# menus by pad, disconnect, fullscreen\nrep(\"Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back.\",\"Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\")\nrep(\"- Pause menu and title only: all other screens are diegetic or overlays with the world visible behind.\",\"- Only the title and pause menus cover the view. Every other screen is in your hands or an overlay with the world visible behind it.\")\nrep(\"Picture (Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in `localStorage`; `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's own panel.\",\n    \"Picture (Fullscreen, for the TV; Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in your own `localStorage` entry and re-applied at boot: `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's panel and stops the engine saving its own copy.\")\nrep(\"(tap works as click).\",\"(tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`).\")\n# attract scope\nrep(\"After **10 seconds with no input on the title or any main-menu screen**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`).\",\"After **10 seconds with no input on the title screen or main menu**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). Settings and About are exempt, because people stop to read them.\")\n# truce rule, acts\nrep(\"| Mile Forty | (0, 40) | Truce town, no-fire zone radius 70 until mission M7. Station, clinic, Tibor's shed, bar, market, notice board |\",\"| Mile Forty | (0, 40) | Truce town, no-fire zone radius 70 until mission M7: inside it your gun is slung and won't fire, and nobody shoots. Station, clinic, Tibor's shed, bar, market, notice board |\")\nrep(\"After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four.\",\"After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\")\nrep(\"| Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | Whoever's left calls in help |\",\"| Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) |\")\nrep(\"Your highest-trust buddy comes along. At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** |\",\"Your highest-trust buddy comes along (with no buddy alive, a Harvest guide named Pell does). At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** |\")\nrep(\"6. M5 (keep its Mags plan in M6 instead).\",\"6. M5 (Mags offers her alternate plan in M6 instead: get the field workers out first, for less pay).\")\n# triggers note\nrep(\"**Movement.** `CharacterController` stays grounded on the heightfield and is right for a grounded soldier.\",\"**Checks.** Use plain distance tests in `fixedUpdate` for sites and pickups: the engine triggers' `tag:'character'` belongs to the platformer hero.\\n\\n**Movement.** `CharacterController` stays grounded on the heightfield and is right for a grounded soldier.\")\n# options\nrep(\"const OPTIONS = withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera:{ preset:'first', fov:62 }, look: LOOK, touch:false, settings:{ button:false, key:false } });\",\"const OPTIONS = withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera:{ preset:'first', fov:62 }, look: LOOK, touch:false, debugKeys:false, settings:{ button:false, key:false } });\")\nrep(\"`withUrlOptions` keeps the review flags (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`, `?look=`), which are useful and harmless.\",\"`withUrlOptions` keeps the review flags (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`, `?look=`), which are useful and harmless. `debugKeys:false` keeps the engine's R, P and M hotkeys from colliding with yours; dev mode has its own tools.\")\n# static suite scope, hub site, byte identity\nrep(\"`Math.random` only in `vendor/`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`; every string\",\"in `src/`: no `Math.random`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`. Every string\")\nrep(\"serve a folder holding the built file (renamed or linked as you like) with `vendor/hub/*` on `127.0.0.1`\",\"copy the built file to `tests/.site/game.html` beside a copy of `vendor/hub/*` (the harness only loads same-origin pages), serve that folder on `127.0.0.1`\")\nrep(\"then for each scenario open `harness.html?game=<file>&<scenario>`\",\"then for each scenario open `harness.html?game=game.html&<scenario>`\")\nrep(\"- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the kit's.\",\"- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the copy in the kit's zip (keep the zip in `vendor/` and compare in the `static` suite).\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPY\npython3 $W/.scratch/spike/patch2.py $W/PLAN.md; wc -w -l $W/PLAN.md","description":"Apply the second set of plan corrections"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4804,"cache_read_input_tokens":514018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4804},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"f9cbae6c-ba11-4199-b824-cfec46cf4feb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:47.468Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCnh2aktGdKoomoLx2P","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BsYebGs3V7MVfQEhy1NpzA":{"command":"W=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work; cat > $W/.scratch/spike/patch2.py <<'PY'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    if a not in s: raise SystemExit('NOT FOUND: '+a[:90])\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\n\n# browser keyboard traps\nrep(\"| Crouch | Circle | B | C or Ctrl |\",\"| Crouch | Circle | B | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab) |\")\nrep(\"| Walk (stick partly tilted or Alt held) | 3.6 | Quiet |\",\"| Walk (stick partly tilted; Caps Lock toggles it on keyboard, never Alt, since Alt+D jumps to the address bar) | 3.6 | Quiet |\")\nrep(\"| Sprint (hold L3/Shift while moving forward) | 7.4 |\",\"| Sprint (click L3 or hold Shift while moving forward) | 7.4 |\")\nrep(\"| Sprint | L3 | LS | Left Shift |\",\"| Sprint | L3 (click) | LS | Left Shift |\")\n# menus by pad, disconnect, fullscreen\nrep(\"Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back.\",\"Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\")\nrep(\"- Pause menu and title only: all other screens are diegetic or overlays with the world visible behind.\",\"- Only the title and pause menus cover the view. Every other screen is in your hands or an overlay with the world visible behind it.\")\nrep(\"Picture (Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in `localStorage`; `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's own panel.\",\n    \"Picture (Fullscreen, for the TV; Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in your own `localStorage` entry and re-applied at boot: `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's panel and stops the engine saving its own copy.\")\nrep(\"(tap works as click).\",\"(tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`).\")\n# attract scope\nrep(\"After **10 seconds with no input on the title or any main-menu screen**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`).\",\"After **10 seconds with no input on the title screen or main menu**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). Settings and About are exempt, because people stop to read them.\")\n# truce rule, acts\nrep(\"| Mile Forty | (0, 40) | Truce town, no-fire zone radius 70 until mission M7. Station, clinic, Tibor's shed, bar, market, notice board |\",\"| Mile Forty | (0, 40) | Truce town, no-fire zone radius 70 until mission M7: inside it your gun is slung and won't fire, and nobody shoots. Station, clinic, Tibor's shed, bar, market, notice board |\")\nrep(\"After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four.\",\"After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\")\nrep(\"| Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | Whoever's left calls in help |\",\"| Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) |\")\nrep(\"Your highest-trust buddy comes along. At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** |\",\"Your highest-trust buddy comes along (with no buddy alive, a Harvest guide named Pell does). At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** |\")\nrep(\"6. M5 (keep its Mags plan in M6 instead).\",\"6. M5 (Mags offers her alternate plan in M6 instead: get the field workers out first, for less pay).\")\n# triggers note\nrep(\"**Movement.** `CharacterController` stays grounded on the heightfield and is right for a grounded soldier.\",\"**Checks.** Use plain distance tests in `fixedUpdate` for sites and pickups: the engine triggers' `tag:'character'` belongs to the platformer hero.\\n\\n**Movement.** `CharacterController` stays grounded on the heightfield and is right for a grounded soldier.\")\n# options\nrep(\"const OPTIONS = withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera:{ preset:'first', fov:62 }, look: LOOK, touch:false, settings:{ button:false, key:false } });\",\"const OPTIONS = withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera:{ preset:'first', fov:62 }, look: LOOK, touch:false, debugKeys:false, settings:{ button:false, key:false } });\")\nrep(\"`withUrlOptions` keeps the review flags (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`, `?look=`), which are useful and harmless.\",\"`withUrlOptions` keeps the review flags (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`, `?look=`), which are useful and harmless. `debugKeys:false` keeps the engine's R, P and M hotkeys from colliding with yours; dev mode has its own tools.\")\n# static suite scope, hub site, byte identity\nrep(\"`Math.random` only in `vendor/`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`; every string\",\"in `src/`: no `Math.random`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`. Every string\")\nrep(\"serve a folder holding the built file (renamed or linked as you like) with `vendor/hub/*` on `127.0.0.1`\",\"copy the built file to `tests/.site/game.html` beside a copy of `vendor/hub/*` (the harness only loads same-origin pages), serve that folder on `127.0.0.1`\")\nrep(\"then for each scenario open `harness.html?game=<file>&<scenario>`\",\"then for each scenario open `harness.html?game=game.html&<scenario>`\")\nrep(\"- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the kit's.\",\"- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the copy in the kit's zip (keep the zip in `vendor/` and compare in the `static` suite).\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPY\npython3 $W/.scratch/spike/patch2.py $W/PLAN.md; wc -w -l $W/PLAN.md","description":"Apply the second set of plan corrections"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BsYebGs3V7MVfQEhy1NpzA","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\n  1128  17134 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work/PLAN.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"62b6cd1d-6494-4224-9385-01cfbc23c5ed","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:47.512Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok\n  1128  17134 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work/PLAN.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BsYebGs3V7MVfQEhy1NpzA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCnhKhAr3iSmca7gib8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PkTcLazfM5K5t6sYNta8ki","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work/planner-exit-interview.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What did you like most about this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"The 'This computer' section. It gives exact browsers, flags, memory behaviour and honest stand-ins for what the machine lacks (no pad, no touch device, nobody to listen), so I could test the plan's risky ideas instead of guessing. The controller-first UX section was the next most useful: it is specific enough to design from. Linking the real engine kit and hub harness meant I could run a spike and tell builders what actually works.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was confusing?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Three things. First, 'for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own': I could not tell whether standalone play must itself have multiplayer or only keep working outside a session, so the plan covers both with solo AI mercs and a same-computer link. Second, most of TASK.md speaks to the builder (title, package, exit interview, chat reply), and only STAGE.md says what the planner does, so I had to work out which lines were mine and which to pass on. Third, the brief says to prefer file:// while the kit's README says ES modules don't load from file://. That only resolves once you try an inline bundle, which does work. A smaller one: 'Music set to 10%' doesn't say which volume it means; I took it as the music channel, not music after the master volume.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Scoping. The brief asks for a complete, polished, no-stubs slice of an open-world shooter, with shared-world netcode, attract mode, dev tools and full story, for builders whose capability and budget I don't know. Keeping it original while still capturing what makes the source distinctive took the most thought, and the map-as-plot twist came from that. The other hard part was finding the engine's first-person traps, which its platformer-minded guide doesn't cover: the 160 m far plane, E and Q turning the camera, pointer lock being reset every frame, and the default pad mapping. I found those by reading the minified bundle and running spikes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What would you change in this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Say plainly which TASK.md lines are for the planner and which are for the builder. Spell out what 'on its own' requires for multiplayer. State the builder's rough budget or capability, so a plan can be scoped to it instead of adding a cut order as a hedge. Add a line to the Sharing section saying planners may use a scratch folder and must delete it afterwards. Note that http.server buffers its port line when piped, because the brief's suggested command hung my script for several minutes. Add to the engine kit's guide a short first-person section covering those traps.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4804,"cache_read_input_tokens":514018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4804},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7680a17-bf1f-4ce7-9c9a-ea1ace567b93","uuid":"0b2ec761-a1e5-4d00-b1c9-6f0d2993c8bd","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:09:57.791Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCnh2aktGdKoomoLx2P","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PkTcLazfM5K5t6sYNta8ki":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211929__x031fe2/work/planner-exit-interview.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What did you like most about this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"The 'This computer' section. It gives exact browsers, flags, memory behaviour and honest stand-ins for what the machine lacks (no pad, no touch device, nobody to listen), so I could test the plan's risky ideas instead of guessing. The controller-first UX section was the next most useful: it is specific enough to design from. Linking the real engine kit and hub harness meant I could run a spike and tell builders what actually works.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was confusing?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Three things. First, 'for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own': I could not tell whether standalone play must itself have multiplayer or only keep working outside a session, so the plan covers both with solo AI mercs and a same-computer link. Second, most of TASK.md speaks to the builder (title, package, exit interview, chat reply), and only STAGE.md says what the planner does, so I had to work out which lines were mine and which to pass on. Third, the brief says to prefer file:// while the kit's README says ES modules don't load from file://. That only resolves once you try an inline bundle, which does work. A smaller one: 'Music set to 10%' doesn't say which volume it means; I took it as the music channel, not music after the master volume.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Scoping. The brief asks for a complete, polished, no-stubs slice of an open-world shooter, with shared-world netcode, attract mode, dev tools and full story, for builders whose capability and budget I don't know. Keeping it original while still capturing what makes the source distinctive took the most thought, and the map-as-plot twist came from that. The other hard part was finding the engine's first-person traps, which its platformer-minded guide doesn't cover: the 160 m far plane, E and Q turning the camera, pointer lock being reset every frame, and the default pad mapping. I found those by reading the minified bundle and running spikes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What would you change in this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Say plainly which TASK.md lines are for the planner and which are for the builder. Spell out what 'on its own' requires for multiplayer. State the builder's rough budget or capability, so a plan can be scoped to it instead of adding a cut order as a hedge. Add a line to the Sharing section saying planners may use a scratch folder and must delete it afterwards. Note that http.server buffers its port line when piped, because the brief's suggested command hung my script for several minutes. Add to the engine kit's guide a short first-person section covering those traps.\"\n  }\n]\n"}}}
